  "deduction": {
    "title": "A Bond Rewritten by Revelation",
    "intro": "Picture yourself entrusted with someone deeply important, then facing a command that ends the bond for the sake of obedience. A revelation reshaped an entire household, and the name at the center of the command was never the one being addressed.",
    "clues": [
      "I stood where personal loyalty had to yield to divine obedience.",
      "I was known in the Messenger's household as an adopted son.",
      "I learned that my marriage became the subject of a revelation addressed to the Messenger of Allah.",
      "I heard the words, 'Keep your wife and fear Allah,' directed toward me.",
      "I then learned that Allah commanded the Messenger of Allah to divorce certain wives, and my own marriage had to end under that command.",
      "I am Zayd ibn Harithah, the adopted son named in Surah Al-Ahzb."
    ],
    "categories": {
